[coal] Use the C++20 standard library in place of Boost

Coal's collision core reaches for Boost in exactly two places, and both
have drop-in equivalents in the C++20 standard library that Coal already
requires:

  boost::math::constants::pi<Scalar>()  ->  std::numbers::pi_v<Scalar>
  boost::span                           ->  std::span

Dropping them lets a consumer build Coal's collision core against Eigen
alone. That matters disproportionately for the `pi` case: including
<boost/math/constants/constants.hpp> from geometric_shapes.h pulls in
over four hundred Boost headers transitively, purely to obtain a
constant.

Drake carries this patch because Drake has no Boost dependency at all and
does not wish to acquire one. It should be upstreamed; nothing here is
Drake-specific.

Note that include/coal/logging.h also includes <boost/log/trivial.hpp>,
but that include and every macro that uses it sit behind
`#ifdef COAL_ENABLE_LOGGING`, which Drake never defines, so no patch is
needed there. The include/coal/third_party/boost/ directory (a backfill
for systems whose Boost predates boost::span) is simply not compiled.

